During installation, a randomly generated password is created for the MySQL root user. To retrieve it, issue the following command:

sudo mysql-strict.rootpass To update this password, start by logging to the MySQL server:

mysql-strict.mysql -u root -p Afterwards, execute the following SQL statement (replace YOUR_NEW_PASS below with a strong password):

ALTER USER 'root'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED WITH caching_sha2_password BY 'YOUR_NEW_PASS'; ---

